 ("Confusing a statement with its converse is one of the most common reasoning errors, in math and in life.",
  "Confusing a statement with its converse is one of the most common reasoning errors, in math and in life. There's also the inverse, not p implies not q: if it didn't rain, the ground isn't wet. That fails for the same reason, sprinklers. The inverse is actually equivalent to the converse, and neither is equivalent to the original."),
